{"type":"FeatureCollection","name":"water_features_1863_epsg3857","crs":{"type":"name","properties":{"name":"urn:ogc:def:crs:EPSG::3857"}},"features":[{"type":"Feature","id":"WF-001","properties":{"id":"WF-001","category":"spring","subtype":"improved spring","name":"Spangler's Spring","name_modern":"","present_1863":true,"period_note":"Improved natural spring at the foot of Culp's Hill; Union and Confederate soldiers drank here; 1870 Tipton photograph shows its probable appearance","sources":[{"cite":"Historical Base Map documentation, Gettysburg NMP (Tilberg and Frantz, 23 June 1958): review of the Warren survey map against the Cope, Bachelder and Official Records sources","sheet_or_page":"documentation grid 3I (pdf p8-9)","url":"https://irma.nps.gov/DataStore/DownloadFile/472812","type":"B","quote_or_paraphrase":"Spangler's Spring in position indicated on the [Warren] map; see the 1940 report 'Proposed Restoration of the Spangler's Spring - Culp's Hill Area' and a Tipton photograph of 1870 for its probable appearance.","key":"NPS-HBM-1958"},{"cite":"Treatment Philosophy: The 1863 Landscape, Gettysburg NMP (NPS, 2004), ch. 2-3 (circulation, fencing, water features)","sheet_or_page":"pdf p77 fig. 2-44","url":"https://irma.nps.gov/DataStore/DownloadFile/472822","type":"B","quote_or_paraphrase":"Spangler's Spring, ca. 1880s-1890s, 'seen here much as it appeared at the time of the battle'.","key":"NPS-TREAT-2004"},{"cite":"OpenStreetMap contributors, Overpass API extract of highway, railway, waterway, barrier and bridge ways (2026-10-19)","sheet_or_page":"way 778735889 (historic=ruins, name Spangler's Spring)","url":"https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright","type":"B","quote_or_paraphrase":"Position of the spring structure as mapped today.","key":"OSM"}],"method":"Position of the OSM-mapped spring ruin (way 778735889 centre); cross-checked in the text against the Warren map position by the 1958 NPS review, not re-measured on the map here.","positional_error_m":20,"conf